    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0137" n="127" xml:id="pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 3/41a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-12T00:00:00-05:00">December 12,
                        1941—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1349. The Chilean Ambassador here has inquired under instructions whether the
                    United States would be ready to go to Santiago instead of Rio if “all the other
                    American Republics agree”. He says that Aranha<anchor n="19a" xml:id="d162-f1"/>
                    has informed the Chilean Foreign Minister that Brazil is ready to forego its
                    right to the seat of the meeting in favor of Chile.</p>
                <p>Please clarify with Aranha and telegraph urgently.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d162-f1" n="19a" xml:id="d162-f1-content">
                <p>Oswaldo Aranha, Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
